  "verbalization": "Iloperidone, a psychotropic agent, is shown to interact with Htr2a and Htr1d, two members of the high-throughput receptor family, through binding interactions. These interactions are supported by a final score of 0.6897 in path_10135 and 0.6366 in path_10136, indicating a plausible biological link. The shared participation of Htr2c in the binding processes of both Htr2a and Htr1d suggests that Htr2c may act as a downstream target or mediator in these pathways. The evidence implies that Iloperidone may modulate the activity of Htr2c through its interaction with Htr2a and Htr1d, potentially influencing serotonin signaling. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Iloperidone could exert its effects on Htr2c, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Htr2c in this context.",
